 "transformation": {
  "a": "Three repeats of five training folds (FigS8_transfer_folds.csv). In each fold: residual = yield - pair mean - training condition mean + training grand mean; both partners' shrunken profiles (sum / (count + 4)) fitted jointly on the training pairs (ten alternating rounds). Fitted ranking: the three largest of training condition mean + the profiles of the target's two molecules (zero for a molecule without training pairs). Raw ranking: the three largest mean raw yields of the training pairs sharing either molecule. Complementary trio: greedy on the training pairs (each step adds the condition that most raises the mean best-of-panel yield). A target is scored when one of its molecules has training pairs and every condition of the panels is measured; per target, the mean over the repeats in which it was scored of best measured yield of the ranked trio minus that of the complementary trio. Product-forming: best measured yield at least 10%. Interval: 5,000 resamples, within each array, of the building blocks of the role whose single-role history explains more held-out residual on the five history folds of Fig. 4A, each with all its targets; pooled mean = sum / count; 2.5th and 97.5th percentiles; default_rng(20260920), arrays in sorted identifier order.",
  "b": "The same folds. For each role and fold: training residual = yield - pair mean - condition mean + grand mean on the training pairs; each molecule's shrunken profile (sum / (count + 4)) over its training pairs; its trio = the three largest of profile + training condition mean. For a fully measured held-out pair whose molecule on that role has training pairs: own = best measured yield of its molecule's trio; substitute = mean over the eligible donors of the best measured yield of each donor's trio. Donors are other molecules of the role with training pairs. Depth and coverage matched: the same number of training pairs, support Jaccard at least 0.95, covered conditions differing by at most one, per-condition counts differing by at most one, normalized count L1 at most 0.05. Exact per-condition counts: identical per-condition counts. Training-activity caliper: matched and mean training yield within 0.05. Closest structural neighbour: matched and ECFP4 (radius 2, 2,048 bits) Tanimoto at least 0.5, the most similar (ties kept). Per target: mean over the folds in which it was scored. Interval: 10,000 whole-array draws, default_rng(20260928), arrays in sorted identifier order; pooled mean = sum / count; 2.5th and 97.5th percentiles.",
  "c": "Analysis arrays (A1). Targets: product-forming pairs whose two molecules each have at least two other product-forming partners, in arrays with at least ten such targets (908); a target is scored when every condition of its panels and of the trio was measured (728). For each target, condition means and slope-adjusted patterns are refitted on the other product-forming pairs of its array. A side's panel = the three conditions with the largest condition mean + that molecule's profile from two of its other pairs (all two-pair subsets, or the 45 with the smallest SHA-256 of the sorted partner identities), ties to the first condition. Best yield = the panel's largest measured yield, averaged over subsets. Difference = owner's panel minus partner's, in percentage points; targets weighted equally. 95% interval: 10,000 draws resampling whole arrays (seed 20261006, arrays in sorted identifier order).",
  "d": "As panel b, in the three arrays where at least 50 targets have an owner with at least six other product-forming partners, with 1, 2, 3, 4 or 6 history partners: five subsets per depth, subset j holding the partners with the smallest SHA-256 of 'target|j|partner'. Gain = best yield of the history-ranked panel minus that of the complementary trio (greedy, fitted on all other pairs of the array), in percentage points. Pointwise 95% intervals: 10,000 draws resampling molecules within the array (seed 20261008 for each curve, molecules in sorted order, the same draws at every depth)."
 },
